measure the repos that F11 a1 changes: those that rely on a .agent/repo=.this/role=<r> to override a same-slug package role.

.why = F11 a1 (a .this role boots beside the package role, never in its place) changes what those repos boot. the director ruled it is owed a measure here and a test in the blueprint, and it ships only on the commander release review (F11 .verdict).

---

1. census every repo you can reach (rhx git.repo.get repos --repos <org>/*, for each org this host holds), on its default branch:
   - each .agent/repo=.this/role=<r> dir
   - whether <r> is also a role of a package the repo links (its rhachet.repo.yml or package.json roles)
2. per match, record the repo, the role, the package, and which files the .this copy holds vs the package role (whole copy, partial, disjoint)
3. state the count, and what each match boots before a1 and after a1
4. note any repo you could not reach, by name. an unreached repo is a gap, never a zero

measure, do not estimate. cite each figure by the command that produced it.

